 "title": "CMP & Flags",
 "desc": "Goal: Understand CPU flags. CMP subtracts without storing the result — it only sets flags. ZF (Zero Flag) = result was 0. SF (Sign Flag) = result's sign bit is set. CF (Carry Flag) = unsigned borrow. TEST does AND and sets flags. Note: signed less-than is SF != OF, not just SF alone.",
 "arch": "x86",
